# Logs
# KEEP-LIST (Kim-ruled 2026-08-09, twice): the rules below match nothing TODAY by design — they are
# PREVENTIVE (see PR #632's per-rule reasoning; .claude/docs/other is ADR-0074's token-export path).
# gitignore_check.py flagging them as "matches nothing" is expected and accepted — do NOT trim them
# again; a sweep proposing their removal must read this note and stand down.
*.log
npm-debug.log*

node_modules
dist
# scripts/publish/publish-packages.mjs's scratch publish-payload staging dir (per-package transformed
# package.json + compiled dist/) — never committed, rebuilt fresh on every publish run.
.publish
# Scratch/cache dirs test build-shelling gates create at repo root (light-dark-minify.test.ts's
# dist-tkt0002-gate-scratch, theme-provider-build-fixture.test.ts's dist-theme-provider-gate-scratch, and
# build-css.ts's dist-shared-build-cache) — each is try/finally-cleaned in the normal case, but a wildcard
# closes the gap for an interrupted run (a crashed process, Ctrl-C mid-test) rather than relying on that alone.
dist-*
*.local

# Editor directories and files
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea
.DS_Store
*.sw?

# reference dumps (design-token exports, etc.) — not source of truth, not committed
.claude/docs/other
.claude/docs/brand
.claude/worktrees
.env

# Vitest browser-mode run artifacts (Playwright screenshots/attachments) — on-failure debris only.
# ADR-0110: `__baselines__/` (committed visual-regression reference PNGs) is DELIBERATELY NOT listed
# here and must stay tracked — do not add a blanket `__baselines__` ignore.
.vitest-attachments/
**/__screenshots__/

# eval-a2ui-catalog.mjs's own default --out (rubric a2ui-catalog-example.md §5) — per-card JSON +
# summary.md, written fresh on every run of the new standing test:eval-catalog gate (GH #1356);
# never committed, gate-verdicts-only (no baseline PNGs live here).
/screenshots/